[agent:thinking] Actually, this is a Hopsworks type mapping issue. In Hopsworks:
[agent:thinking] - `int` = 32-bit integer
[agent:thinking] - `bigint` = 64-bit integer
[agent:thinking] 
[agent:thinking] When pandas reads integers from JSON, it defaults to `int64`, which maps to `bigint` in Hopsworks. The simplest solution is to delete and recreate the profiles feature group with `credit_score:bigint`. I should also apply the same fix to `sessions_7d` in the activity feature group, since it has the same issue. Going forward, I'll use `bigint` for all integer types when creating feature groups to avoid this mismatch.
